---
import Case from '../../layouts/Case.astro';

// Draft wording, for the owner to review before publishing. Mirrors the public LinkedIn post.
const glance: [string, string][] = [
  ['What', 'A learning method'],
  ['Built with', 'Claude'],
  ['Status', 'Done, and repeatable'],
  ['Shown', 'Story on LinkedIn'],
];
---

<Case title="Certified in under a week" glance={glance} link="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/naomei_claude-certified-architect-foundations-share-7498394916474048517-ola7/" linkLabel="Read the story on LinkedIn">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <h1>Certified in <span class="mut">under a week</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      From zero architecture knowledge to passing the Claude Certified Architect – Foundations exam in just under a week.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Where it started</h2>
  <p>
    I started with no architecture knowledge, and under a week to go from there to passing.
  </p>

  <h2>What I did</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Take mock exams and drills to find the gaps.</li>
    <li>Feed the wrong answers back into Claude.</li>
    <li>Turn them into a personalised study plan and a cheat sheet.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What I learned</h2>
  <p>
    Mistakes are the most useful input you have. Used well, an AI assistant can turn them into a plan, and a plan beats trying to cover everything. It is the same pattern as the rest of my work: spot the need, draft quickly, check it, and feed what went wrong back in.
  </p>
</Case>
